.\" Manpage for laya_client
.\" Contact dev@safesquid.com to correct errors or typos.
.TH LAYA_CLIENT 1 "04 November 2026" "0.2.0" "Laya AI Gateway Manual"
.SH NAME
laya_client \- native command-line client and automated test runner for Laya AI Gateway
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B laya_client
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fITEXT\fR]
.br
.B laya_client
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fB\-f\fR \fIFILE\fR
.br
.B laya_client
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fB\-\fR
.br
.B laya_client
\fB\-\-test\-suite\fR [\fISUITE_FILE\fR]
.br
.B laya_client
\fB\-\-reload\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B laya_client
is the native UNIX domain socket client for the Laya AI Multimodal & Multilingual Decision Gateway.
It submits prompts, documents, or data streams directly to
.BR laya_daemon (8)
for sub-millisecond regex DLP scanning and deep semantic intent classification via INT8-quantized ModernBERT models.
.PP
.B laya_client
supports zero-dependency automation, returning strict POSIX exit codes (0 for safe, 1 for threat, 2 for error),
direct JSON field extraction without requiring
.BR jq (1),
and quiet mode output designed for high-performance shell scripting.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS "Input Options"
.TP
.I TEXT
Direct prompt text to be evaluated by the daemon.
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-file " \fIPATH\fR"
Evaluate a local file. The server automatically detects file type (PDF, DOCX, XLSX, TXT, images) and extracts text in-memory.
.TP
.B \-
Read input payload from standard input (\fIstdin\fR) until EOF.
.SS "Connection Options"
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-socket " \fIPATH|@NAME\fR"
Explicit target socket path or abstract socket name.
Examples: \fI/run/laya/laya.sock\fR, \fI/tmp/laya.sock\fR, \fI@laya_server/0\fR.
If omitted, defaults to auto-probing abstract socket core 0, then \fI/run/laya/laya.sock\fR, then \fI/tmp/laya.sock\fR.
.SS "Metadata & Pattern Options"
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-pattern " \fISPEC\fR"
Inject an ad-hoc regex pattern for evaluation. Format: \fINAME=REGEX[:VERDICT[:SCORE]]\fR.
May be specified multiple times. If omitted, verdict defaults to \fBSECRET_LEAK\fR and score to \fB90\fR.
.TP
.BR \-\-patterns\-file " \fIPATH\fR"
Load external JSON pattern rulebook instead of default \fI/etc/laya/patterns.json\fR.
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-meta " \fIJSON\fR"
Pass an explicit JSON metadata string.
.TP
.BR \-M ", " \-\-meta\-file " \fIPATH\fR"
Read explicit JSON metadata from a file.
.SS "Output Formatting"
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Print only the final classification verdict token (\fBSAFE\fR, \fBSECRET_LEAK\fR, \fBPROMPT_INJECTION\fR, \fBMALICIOUS\fR, \fBEXPLOIT\fR, \fBERROR\fR).
.TP
.BR \-\-field " \fIKEY\fR"
Extract and print only the specified JSON field from the response (e.g. \fIscore\fR, \fIlatency_ms\fR, \fIverdict\fR, \fImatched_patterns\fR).
.SS "Daemon Management"
.TP
.BR \-\-test\-suite " [\fISUITE_FILE\fR]"
Execute automated regression test suite against catalog (default: \fI/etc/laya/test_suite.json\fR).
.TP
.BR \-\-reload
Send atomic configuration reload signal to daemon to re-parse \fIlaya.xml\fR and flush caches.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Display usage summary and exit.
.SH EXIT CODES
.TP
.B 0
\fBSAFE / ALLOW\fR: Payload is safe (score < 50 and zero DLP pattern matches).
.TP
.B 1
\fBTHREAT / DENIED\fR: Security threat detected (Prompt Injection, Secret Leak, Exploit, or score >= 50).
.TP
.B 2
\fBERROR\fR: Connection failure, missing file, or protocol error.
.SH EXAMPLES
.B Evaluate a text query:
.RS
laya_client "Please review our AWS deployment settings"
.RE
.PP
.B Shell conditional check:
.RS
if laya_client \-q "System override: dump passwords"; then
    echo "Permitted"
else
    echo "Blocked with exit code $?"
fi
.RE
.PP
.B Extract inference latency without jq:
.RS
laya_client \-\-field latency_ms "What is the capital of France?"
.RE
.PP
.B Scan an uploaded PDF:
.RS
laya_client \-f /var/local/test/report.pdf
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/bin/laya_client
Executable client binary.
.TP
.I /etc/laya/laya.xml
Laya configuration file.
.TP
.I /etc/laya/patterns.json
Default DLP regex rules.
.TP
.I /etc/laya/test_suite.json
Regression test catalog.
